UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) AWS Lambda is a serverless compute service, meaning users do not provision or pay directly for EC2 instances, and while data may be stored in other AWS services, it is not a primary component of Lambda''s execution pricing model. Option B (correct) AWS Lambda''s primary pricing components are indeed the number of times a function is invoked (requests) and the total compute duration, which is a combination of execution time and allocated memory, expressed as GB-seconds. Option C (incorrect) While network data transfer can incur costs for Lambda functions, particularly for outbound traffic to the internet or cross-region, it is considered a secondary or ancillary charge, not one of the two primary components directly tied to the function''s execution. Option D (incorrect) The storage used for the function code and its associated layers is a very minor and often free-tier cost within AWS Lambda, not a primary component of its execution-based pricing model that scales with invocations and duration.'
WHERE id = 'q_63_m_63_1_34';

