UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) A NAT Gateway enables instances in a private subnet to initiate outbound internet connections, but it does not allow inbound connections from internet users to access an application. Option B (correct) An Internet Gateway is essential as it provides the necessary connection between your Virtual Private Cloud and the internet, allowing internet users to send traffic to your application. Option C (incorrect) A private subnet''s routing table does not direct traffic to an Internet Gateway, meaning resources within it cannot be directly accessed by internet users. Option D (correct) A public subnet is required because it has a route to an Internet Gateway, allowing resources deployed within it to be directly reachable by internet users. Option E (incorrect) VPC Peering establishes a private connection between two VPCs, which is unrelated to enabling internet users to access an application within a single VPC.'
