-- question_id: q_62_m_62_6_47
-- answer_correct: True | verified_indices: [1, 2] | confidence: 100%
UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) S3 Transfer Acceleration uses CloudFront''s global edge network to speed up data transfers to and from S3 buckets, focusing on performance rather than data protection from accidental deletion or cost management. Option B (correct) S3 Versioning keeps multiple versions of an object in the same bucket, allowing you to retrieve previous versions of an object if it is accidentally deleted or overwritten, directly protecting data from accidental deletion. Option C (correct) S3 Lifecycle Policies define rules to automatically transition objects to different, potentially cheaper, storage classes (e.g., S3 Glacier) or to expire them after a certain period, directly helping to manage storage costs over time. Option D (incorrect) S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) automatically replicates objects to a destination bucket in a different AWS Region for disaster recovery and compliance, which protects against regional outages but does not directly prevent accidental deletion within the source bucket or manage storage costs in the way lifecycle policies do. Option E (incorrect) S3 Object Lock prevents objects from being deleted or overwritten for a fixed amount of time or indefinitely, providing Write Once Read Many (WORM) storage for compliance, which protects against accidental deletion but does not directly manage storage costs over time.'
WHERE id = 'q_62_m_62_6_47';

