UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (correct) Spot Instances are ideal for the data processing jobs because they allow for significant cost savings (up to 90% compared to On-Demand) for fault-tolerant, flexible, and interruption-tolerant workloads that are not time-sensitive. Option B (incorrect) Running both workloads on On-Demand Instances is not the most cost-effective approach as On-Demand pricing is the most expensive EC2 option and does not leverage the cost-saving opportunities available for interruptible or stable, long-term workloads. Option C (incorrect) Using AWS Lambda for data processing jobs is not an EC2 pricing model and would involve a different serverless compute architecture, whereas the question explicitly states processing using "Amazon EC2 instances" and asks for EC2 pricing models. Option D (correct) Purchasing Amazon EC2 Reserved Instances is highly cost-effective for the stable production web application, offering substantial discounts (up to 75% off On-Demand) for a one-year or three-year commitment to predictable and continuously available EC2 workloads. Option E (incorrect) While AWS Savings Plans also offer cost savings for stable compute usage, Amazon EC2 Reserved Instances (Option D) are specifically targeted for stable EC2 instance commitments, and selecting both for the same workload would be redundant given the requirement to choose only two distinct pricing models.'
WHERE id = 'q_63_m_63_1_90';

