    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) In-place deployment updates existing application instances directly, which can lead to downtime during the update process and makes quick rollbacks challenging as the original state must be individually restored on each instance. Option B (correct) Blue/green deployment creates an entirely new, identical environment (green) for the new model version, allows for full testing, and enables traffic to be gradually shifted from the old environment (blue) to the new one using services like Amazon Route 53 weighted routing or Application Load Balancer target group weights, ensuring minimal downtime and instant rollbacks by simply switching traffic back to the blue environment. Option C (incorrect) Rollback deployment is an action taken to revert to a previous application version in case of issues, not a strategy for initially deploying a new version and gradually shifting traffic. Option D (incorrect) Snapshot deployment typically refers to deploying an application or database from a saved image or state, which is a method of provisioning but not a traffic-shifting deployment strategy that inherently minimizes downtime or enables quick rollbacks with gradual traffic shifts.'
