-- question_id: q_17_m_17_1_68
-- answer_correct: True | verified_indices: [1] | confidence: 100%
UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) Concept drift refers to a change in the relationship between input features and the target variable, meaning the underlying problem the model is trying to solve has evolved, which is distinct from a change solely in the input data distribution observed by a data scientist through Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor. Option B (correct) Data drift occurs when the statistical properties of the incoming inference data change over time compared to the data the model was trained on, which is precisely what Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor is designed to detect when a data scientist observes a shift in the distribution of incoming inference data. Option C (incorrect) Bias drift refers to a change in the fairness of the model''s predictions over time, where certain demographic groups might experience disparate impact, which is a specific aspect distinct from a general shift in overall data distribution monitored by Amazon SageMaker Clarify for potential fairness issues. Option D (incorrect) Model quality drift describes a degradation in the model''s performance metrics, such as accuracy or precision, which is typically a consequence of other types of drift like data drift or concept drift, rather than the primary observed cause of a changed input data distribution that Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor tracks.'
WHERE id = 'q_17_m_17_1_68';

-- question_id: q_17_m_17_1_75
-- answer_correct: True | verified_indices: [3] | confidence: 100%
