    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) Data quality monitoring in Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor detects changes in the statistical properties of the input data itself, such as schema, data types, missing values, or distributions, not how the model interprets or utilizes those features. Option B (incorrect) Model quality monitoring tracks the performance of the model over time using metrics like accuracy, precision, recall, or RMSE by comparing predictions to ground truth labels, rather than analyzing the internal contribution of individual features. Option C (incorrect) Bias drift monitoring, often integrated with SageMaker Clarify, specifically focuses on detecting changes in fairness metrics or performance disparities across different sensitive attribute groups over time, not the overall importance of all features to the model''s predictions. Option D (correct) Feature attribution drift monitoring is specifically designed to detect if the relative importance or contribution of features to a model''s predictions, as quantified by explainability techniques like SHAP, has changed over time, directly addressing the concept of feature importance shifts.'
WHERE id = 'q_17_m_17_1_75';

