    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) Normalization scales numerical features to a standard range, which improves model performance but does not reduce the number of features in a dataset; AWS SageMaker''s built-in algorithms often benefit from normalized data, but the feature count remains the same. Option B (correct) Principal Component Analysis (PCA) is a dimensionality reduction technique that transforms features into a smaller set of principal components, thereby reducing the number of features while retaining maximum variance; AWS SageMaker provides a built-in PCA algorithm specifically for this purpose. Option C (incorrect) Encoding categorical variables converts non-numerical data into a numerical format, often increasing the number of features (e.g., one-hot encoding), rather than reducing them; AWS Glue DataBrew offers encoding transformations but these typically expand the feature space. Option D (correct) Correlation analysis identifies highly correlated features, allowing practitioners to remove redundant ones without significant loss of information, thereby reducing the number of features; AWS SageMaker Data Wrangler can be used to visualize correlations and inform feature selection decisions to reduce the dataset''s dimensionality. Option E (incorrect) Binning groups continuous numerical data into discrete intervals, which transforms an existing feature but does not reduce the total count of features in the dataset; AWS Glue DataBrew offers binning transformations, but they do not lead to a reduction in the number of features.'
