UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (correct) SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Over-sampling Technique) is a correct technique as it addresses class imbalance by generating synthetic samples for the minority class, a preprocessing step often executed in a SageMaker Processing job or a SageMaker notebook instance before training a model with services like Amazon SageMaker. Option B (incorrect) Normalization is an incorrect technique because it scales numerical features to a standard range (e.g., 0-1 or Z-score) to improve model convergence and performance, a common data preprocessing step in Amazon SageMaker for algorithms like Linear Learner, but it does not change the distribution of classes. Option C (correct) Oversampling is a correct technique because it addresses class imbalance by increasing the number of instances in the minority class, which can be implemented as a data preparation step using AWS Glue or a SageMaker Processing job before feeding data to a model in Amazon SageMaker. Option D (correct) Undersampling is a correct technique because it addresses class imbalance by reducing the number of instances in the majority class, a strategy that can be applied during data preprocessing using custom scripts in a SageMaker notebook instance or a SageMaker Processing job before model training. Option E (incorrect) Feature scaling is an incorrect technique because it adjusts the range of features to a common scale, which is crucial for the performance of many machine learning algorithms like K-Means or PCA in Amazon SageMaker, but it does not modify the underlying class distribution in the dataset.'
