UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (correct) Amazon SageMaker Clarify helps detect and quantify bias in training data by analyzing sensitive attributes and fairness metrics before model training and also provides model explainability. Option B (incorrect) Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth is a data labeling service used to create high-quality training datasets, but it does not detect or quantify bias within the data. Option C (correct) AWS Glue DataBrew can detect potential bias by profiling data characteristics, distributions, and imbalances across sensitive attributes through its data preparation and analysis capabilities. Option D (incorrect) Amazon S3 is an object storage service used to store datasets but provides no capabilities for detecting or quantifying bias within the stored data. Option E (incorrect) AWS Lake Formation is used to build, secure, and manage data lakes, primarily focusing on data access control and governance, not on detecting or quantifying bias in data.'
