    explanation = 'Option A (correct) Warm Standby is the correct strategy because it involves maintaining a scaled-down but operational environment in a separate region, ready to be scaled up to full capacity during a disaster, using services like cross-region RDS read replicas or EC2 instances with replicated data. Option B (incorrect) Cold Disaster Recovery is incorrect because it involves provisioning infrastructure only after a disaster occurs, meaning no functional duplicate environment exists beforehand, which is contrary to the question''s description. Option C (incorrect) A Cold Disaster Recovery involves regularly backing up data to another region and only provisioning infrastructure when a disaster occurs, which results in the longest recovery time objectives (RTO) but is the most cost-effective solution is incorrect because while it accurately describes Cold Disaster Recovery, the question''s scenario explicitly describes maintaining an already provisioned, scaled-down environment, which Cold DR does not. Option D (incorrect) Backup and Restore is incorrect because it focuses on recreating the environment and restoring data from backups after a disaster, rather than maintaining a continuously running, scaled-down duplicate environment beforehand, which leads to a longer recovery time than a Warm Standby.'
