    explanation = 'Option [0] Cold HDD (sc1) is incorrect because it is designed for infrequently accessed, large, sequential workloads and offers the lowest per-GB cost, making it entirely unsuitable for the high IOPS and low latency requirements of transactional databases. Option [1] Throughput Optimized HDD (st1) is incorrect because, while it provides higher throughput than sc1, it is optimized for large, sequential workloads and does not deliver the low latency and high IOPS performance critical for demanding transactional database applications. Option [2] General Purpose SSD (gp3) is incorrect because while it offers a good balance of price and performance and allows independent scaling of IOPS and throughput, it typically does not provide the consistent ultra-low latency and peak IOPS required by the most demanding, mission-critical transactional databases compared to Provisioned IOPS SSDs. Option [3] Provisioned IOPS SSD (io2) is correct because it is specifically designed for I/O-intensive, mission-critical applications that require consistent high performance, extremely low latency, and high IOPS, making it the ideal choice for large transactional databases.'
