    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) S3 Lifecycle Policies are used to automatically manage object storage classes and to expire (delete) objects, which does not protect against accidental deletion or modification but rather automates deletion. Option B (incorrect) S3 Cross-Region Replication creates copies of objects in a different AWS region for disaster recovery, but it replicates changes including accidental deletions or modifications from the source to the destination bucket. Option C (correct) S3 Versioning protects against accidental deletion or modification by keeping multiple versions of an object, allowing recovery to a previous state if an object is overwritten or restoring a deleted object by removing a delete marker. Option D (incorrect) S3 Object Lock prevents objects from being deleted or overwritten for a fixed or indefinite period, but while it provides strong immutability and prevents changes, S3 Versioning is the foundational feature designed for recovering from accidental user errors by maintaining a full history of object states.'
