    explanation = 'Option A (correct) S3 Lifecycle Policies allow you to define rules to automatically transition objects to different S3 storage classes (like S3 Standard-IA, S3 Glacier, or S3 Glacier Deep Archive) or expire them after a specified period, directly addressing the need to reduce costs for infrequently accessed backups. Option B (incorrect) S3 Versioning helps maintain multiple versions of an object within the same bucket for data recovery, but it typically increases storage costs by keeping more data and does not automatically move objects to lower-cost storage classes. Option C (incorrect) S3 Transfer Acceleration uses Amazon CloudFront''s global edge network to speed up data transfers to and from S3 buckets, which is a performance feature for uploads and downloads, not a cost-saving feature for storage classes. Option D (incorrect) S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) automatically copies objects between S3 buckets in different AWS Regions for disaster recovery or compliance, which adds to storage costs by duplicating data and does not automatically transition objects to cheaper storage classes within a single bucket''s lifecycle.'
