UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) IAM access keys are credentials used for programmatic access to AWS, not a mechanism to define or limit the maximum permissions an IAM principal can have. Option B (correct) IAM permissions boundaries are an advanced feature used to set the maximum permissions an identity-based policy can grant to an IAM user or role, effectively preventing them from performing actions like deleting critical S3 buckets even if their attached policies would otherwise allow it. Option C (incorrect) IAM group policies are identity-based policies that grant permissions to all users within a group, but they define what permissions users have, not the maximum permissions they can ever be granted beyond what a boundary allows. Option D (incorrect) IAM roles are identities that define a set of permissions for entities that need to make AWS API calls, but they are principals themselves and can have permission boundaries applied to them, rather than being the feature that sets the maximum permission boundary.'
