    explanation = 'Option 0 (incorrect) A Spread Placement Group places instances on distinct underlying hardware to minimize correlated failures, which would increase network latency between instances instead of reducing it. Option 1 (incorrect) A Partition Placement Group spreads instances across different logical partitions to reduce the impact of hardware failures, which is not designed for the extremely low-latency communication required by HPC within a single AZ. Option 2 (correct) A Cluster Placement Group packs instances closely together within a single Availability Zone on the same underlying network hardware to achieve extremely low-latency network performance and high throughput, which is ideal for HPC tasks. Option 3 (incorrect) A Dedicated Host provides physical EC2 servers for dedicated use and addresses licensing requirements, but it does not inherently guarantee extremely low inter-instance network latency across multiple hosts for HPC as effectively as a Cluster Placement Group.'
