    explanation = 'Option A (correct) AWS Site-to-Site VPN establishes a secure, private encrypted tunnel over the public internet to connect an on-premises network directly to an AWS VPC. Option B (incorrect) Amazon Connect is a cloud-based contact center service used for customer service operations, not for establishing network connectivity between on-premises data centers and AWS VPCs. Option C (correct) AWS Direct Connect provides a dedicated physical network connection from an on-premises data center to an AWS Direct Connect location, offering private, high-bandwidth connectivity directly to AWS VPCs, bypassing the public internet. Option D (incorrect) AWS Client VPN is a managed VPN service designed to provide secure access for individual users (clients) from their devices to AWS resources and on-premises networks, not for connecting an entire on-premises data center to AWS. Option E (incorrect) Amazon VPC Peering enables private network connectivity between two Amazon VPCs, whether in the same or different AWS accounts, but it does not facilitate connections between an on-premises data center and an AWS VPC.'
