    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) AWS CodeBuild is incorrect because it is primarily a build service that compiles code, runs tests, and produces artifacts, functioning as a stage within a larger CI/CD pipeline, but it does not orchestrate the entire workflow from code commit to deployment. Option B (correct) AWS CodePipeline is correct because it is the dedicated AWS service for orchestrating and automating the entire release process, integrating with source control systems, build services like CodeBuild, and deployment services like CodeDeploy to manage the complete CI/CD workflow from commit to deployment. Option C (incorrect) AWS CodeDeploy is incorrect because it is a deployment service that automates application deployments to various compute services and manages deployment strategies, but it does not encompass the entire CI/CD workflow orchestration, build, or source control integration aspects. Option D (incorrect) AWS Lambda is incorrect because it is a serverless compute service for running event-driven code and can be a deployment target or used for specific tasks within a pipeline, but it is not designed to orchestrate a complete CI/CD workflow itself.'
