-- question_id: q_36_m_36_4_11
-- answer_correct: True | verified_indices: [2] | confidence: 100%
UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) because in-place deployment replaces the application on existing instances, which typically involves stopping and restarting the application on each instance, leading to downtime during the update cycle for those specific instances and making rollback a process of reapplying the old version rather than an instant switch. Option B (incorrect) because an all-at-once deployment updates all target instances simultaneously, resulting in a complete service outage for the duration of the deployment process, which is far from minimal downtime. Option C (correct) because blue/green deployment provisions a completely new set of instances with the new application version, keeps the old environment live, and shifts traffic only after the new environment is fully validated, ensuring near-zero downtime and providing an immediate rollback by simply routing traffic back to the original environment. Option D (incorrect) because a rolling update, while reducing overall downtime compared to all-at-once, still incurs individual instance downtime as batches are updated, and rollback typically requires another update process to revert instances to the previous version rather than an instant traffic switch.'
WHERE id = 'q_36_m_36_4_11';

-- question_id: q_36_m_36_1_12
-- answer_correct: True | verified_indices: [1] | confidence: 100%
