UPDATE public.question
SET
    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) This describes a mutable deployment where existing infrastructure components are modified in place, which is the opposite of an immutable deployment where components are never changed after creation. Option B (incorrect) Rollback in an immutable deployment typically involves reverting traffic to the previous, unmodified set of instances or deploying the prior version''s immutable image to new instances, not by reverting code on the same instances. Option C (incorrect) Preserving application state across instance reboots is an architectural concern related to application design (e.g., using external data stores like Amazon RDS or DynamoDB for stateless applications), not a key characteristic of the immutable deployment process itself. Option D (correct) In an immutable deployment, new instances are launched with the updated application code or configuration, traffic is shifted to these new instances, and then the old instances are gracefully terminated, ensuring no instance is ever modified after deployment.'
WHERE id = 'q_36_m_36_4_15';

