    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) AWS Systems Manager Inventory collects data about the applications, network configurations, and other details on managed instances at a point in time, but it does not provide a continuous historical record of all configuration changes for auditing purposes across various AWS resources like S3 buckets. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudFormation Drift Detection identifies when actual resource configurations differ from their defined CloudFormation stack templates, but it is not a service for continuous historical recording of all configuration changes across all AWS resources for auditing. Option C (incorrect) AWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS, focusing on provisioning and governance rather than continuous monitoring and recording of configuration changes for auditing. Option D (correct) AWS Config continuously monitors and records the configuration changes of supported AWS resources like EC2 instances and S3 buckets, providing a detailed configuration history that is essential for security auditing, compliance, and operational troubleshooting.'
