    explanation = 'Option A (incorrect) CloudFormation Change Sets allow users to preview the proposed changes to a stack before execution, which is a safety feature for managing updates but does not facilitate consistent deployment across multiple accounts and Regions. Option B (correct) CloudFormation StackSets enable the deployment of a single CloudFormation template as a stack instance across multiple AWS accounts and Regions simultaneously, perfectly addressing the need for consistent and efficient baseline resource deployment. Option C (incorrect) CloudFormation Custom Resources allow extending CloudFormation''s capabilities with custom logic using AWS Lambda or SNS, which is useful for provisioning unsupported resources but does not inherently provide a mechanism for multi-account, multi-Region deployment. Option D (correct) CloudFormation Nested Stacks enable the modularization of templates by allowing a stack to reference other stacks, creating reusable components for common baseline resources that can then be deployed consistently by a root stack, often in conjunction with StackSets for multi-account/Region distribution. Option E (incorrect) CloudFormation Drift Detection identifies configuration changes made to resources outside of CloudFormation, which is crucial for maintaining compliance and consistency post-deployment but does not address the initial requirement of consistently deploying infrastructure.'
